{"author":{"id":"0fb62b7075a4219f84b4bf8c9c235af1632f3fa4b63ca899f025ad8215a930fd"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778070874,"nonce":"tWB966yS4paLMe0TEOU7mnVYoCk=","title":"There is no machine-readable data dictionary describing the 15 columns of data/masters.RDS, their types, allowed values, or the provenance of each (which `dc.*` Brage field they were derived from). The implicit specification lives in validate_masters() (R/utils.R) and the loose value lists in R/variable_defs.R, both of which are easy to drift from.","message":"For a dataset meant to be shared openly, a data dictionary is the minimum self-description.\n\n- Add data/data_dictionary.csv (or YAML) with one row per variable: name · type · description · allowed values (where applicable) · source Brage field(s) · notes.\n- Document the conventions explicitly: `||` as separator inside `authors` and abstract fields; `full_text_available` as `\"Ja\"`/`\"Nei\"`/NA; GLU vocabulary; ISO-639-2 vs free-text in `language`.\n- Cover known systematic missingness (Nord abstracts, INN/Hivolda GLU=NA, UiT 207 missing year+author).\n- Generate it from R/variable_defs.R / validate_masters() metadata if practical, so it stays in sync; otherwise check it in CI against the actual columns.\n- Reference it from README.md.\n\nR/variable_defs.R already lists `master_levels` for GLU, language, pdf, school_subject — promote that to the source of truth and have validate_masters() consume it. The current `language` column also contains literal `\"N/A\"` strings (5 rows) that should be NA — fold that normalisation in here.\n\nPrerequisite for the portable-export bug (separate): the CSV/Parquet copies should ship the dictionary alongside them.","files":null}]}